1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:07,198
Japan, 1635. The shogunate makes the lords live in Edo every other year.

2
00:00:08,498 --> 00:00:12,221
So every year, each lord makes the journey, to Edo or home.

3
00:00:13,921 --> 00:00:20,412
A small lord brings about a hundred people. The greatest bring two thousand or more, with all the lord will need.

4
00:00:22,312 --> 00:00:29,544
On the Tōkaidō, each station keeps a hundred porters and a hundred horses for everyone on the road, and an inn for lords.

5
00:00:31,444 --> 00:00:35,482
A procession of three hundred, arriving unannounced, would find too few.

6
00:00:36,582 --> 00:00:42,262
Its loads would wait, and the inn might be taken. Each day on the road costs the domain dearly.

7
00:00:43,962 --> 00:00:50,292
So the stations need to know what's coming, and when, and the domain needs the journey planned before it starts.

8
00:00:52,192 --> 00:00:55,903
Before the lord sets out, his officials plan the journey end to end.

9
00:00:56,803 --> 00:01:00,760
They list who goes, within the limits the shogunate sets for his rank.

10
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:09,591
And they send a notice ahead to every station: how many porters and horses, on which day, and where the lord will rest and sleep.

11
00:01:11,691 --> 00:01:17,056
A day or two before, a board with his name goes up at the inn, and nobody else may stay there.

12
00:01:18,956 --> 00:01:25,702
So each station knows days ahead what's coming, and if its own aren't enough, calls on nearby villages in time.

13
00:01:27,402 --> 00:01:33,028
The loads go on, station to station, on the porters and horses that serve every traveller.

14
00:01:34,328 --> 00:01:37,767
One road for everyone, and each journey planned end to end.

15
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:46,051
At the utility, three teams start three pieces of the social tariff, and nobody has drawn how they join.

16
00:01:47,351 --> 00:01:54,185
So Sipho Dlamini, a solution architect, designs it end to end, on the platform everyone shares.

17
00:02:01,285 --> 00:02:09,684
In November, the government sets a social tariff: from the first of July, a discount for every eligible household, with no forms.

18
00:02:11,184 --> 00:02:15,131
Only the social services agency knows who is eligible.

19
00:02:16,431 --> 00:02:21,923
By December, billing's vendor offers to do it all inside billing, in its October release.

20
00:02:23,423 --> 00:02:27,146
The data team starts its own table of eligible households.

21
00:02:28,246 --> 00:02:31,969
And IT orders a server, to receive the agency's files.

22
00:02:33,469 --> 00:02:38,368
Soon there are two lists of who's eligible, and nobody has drawn how the pieces join.

23
00:02:40,268 --> 00:02:44,257
Nobody was careless. Each team did what it could see from where it stood.

24
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:49,008
The head of retail asks for one design, in a ticket.

25
00:02:52,708 --> 00:02:56,547
The ticket goes to Sipho, who works beside two other architects.

26
00:02:57,847 --> 00:03:02,958
Tomás, the enterprise architect, keeps the map: what changes, and who must agree.

27
00:03:04,658 --> 00:03:09,009
Ravi, who leads the platform, builds what every solution shares, once.

28
00:03:10,709 --> 00:03:16,719
And Sipho designs one solution, end to end: from the agency's answer to the line on a bill.

29
00:03:18,619 --> 00:03:25,182
What every team could use, Ravi builds into the platform. What would change the map, Tomás is asked first.

30
00:03:27,282 --> 00:03:33,140
As on the Tōkaidō, the shogunate kept the road, and each domain planned its own journey on it.

31
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:41,997
Sipho starts with the context: everything the solution touches, on one page.

32
00:03:43,497 --> 00:03:49,483
The agency, the customer system, billing, the call centre, and the households, who get a letter and a bill.

33
00:03:51,583 --> 00:03:54,816
In the middle, the solution itself, on the data platform.

34
00:03:56,316 --> 00:04:02,500
Out of scope for now: tenants whose account is in a landlord's name. Their route comes later in the year.

35
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:08,915
Fixed: ready by the first of July, under the three rules already agreed.

36
00:04:12,815 --> 00:04:17,757
Then, the qualities it must have, each with a measure a design can be tested against.

37
00:04:19,057 --> 00:04:22,626
A standard lists nine. Sipho picks the three that matter here.

38
00:04:24,126 --> 00:04:29,726
Security: only billing's job reads the agency's answers, and every read is logged.

39
00:04:31,626 --> 00:04:37,322
Reliability: every bill run has answers, the latest, or the last ones if new ones are late.

40
00:04:39,222 --> 00:04:44,687
Easy to change: when the agency changes its file, the exchange changes within a week.

41
00:04:46,587 --> 00:04:49,760
Speed hardly matters: the match runs once a month.

42
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:57,834
Sipho draws two options, and tests both against the same three measures.

43
00:04:59,134 --> 00:05:02,347
The first does it all inside billing, as the vendor offered.

44
00:05:03,647 --> 00:05:11,852
But billing logs who changes a record, not who reads it. Every change waits for the vendor's next release. And it's ready in October.

45
00:05:13,952 --> 00:05:19,653
The second keeps the agency's answers on the data platform, as a data product of retail's.

46
00:05:20,953 --> 00:05:28,679
Before each bill run, billing asks through the integration platform for only what a bill needs: on the tariff, and from which date.

47
00:05:30,579 --> 00:05:36,193
The catalogue checks and logs every read, a change is a pull request, and it's ready in May.

48
00:05:38,093 --> 00:05:44,920
Its risk: billing now depends on the platform. So billing asks the day before each run, and keeps what it got.

49
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:53,112
Sipho writes the decision down, in a record kept with the solution's code.

50
00:05:54,412 --> 00:06:00,148
Decided: the answers on the platform, the discount in billing. Considered: all of it in billing.

51
00:06:01,848 --> 00:06:08,952
Why: every read logged, a change in days, and ready by May. The consequence: billing asks the day before.

52
00:06:10,852 --> 00:06:19,989
Ama checks it against the principles: use what we have before we build, and customer information stays with the business that collected it. Both hold.

53
00:06:21,889 --> 00:06:26,403
Sipho, Ravi and the head of retail agree, and the record says accepted.

54
00:06:28,103 --> 00:06:32,459
A year on, whoever asks why billing doesn't do it all will find the answer here.

55
00:06:36,359 --> 00:06:40,405
Then Sipho counts the parts. Of ten, six already exist.

56
00:06:41,705 --> 00:06:50,328
Retail's customer accounts, a job from the platform's template, its connectors, the catalogue's masks and log, the gateway, and monitoring.

57
00:06:52,228 --> 00:06:58,017
Four are new: the match and its answers, a discount step in billing, the letter, and sending a file out.

58
00:06:59,917 --> 00:07:07,844
Every team will need to send files out. So Ravi builds that once, into the platform. The regulator's reports use it next.

59
00:07:09,944 --> 00:07:14,345
On the Tōkaidō, the stations were already there. Only the journey was new.

60
00:07:18,245 --> 00:07:27,420
Each team hears its part months ahead: the platform team, Yasmin's integration team, retail, for the letter and the call centre, and billing's vendor.

61
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:32,318
The vendor puts the discount step in its April release.

62
00:07:33,818 --> 00:07:38,350
As a notice went ahead to every station, each team knows what's coming, and when.

63
00:07:42,250 --> 00:07:46,441
It's built by May, and tested with a sample from the agency in June.

64
00:07:47,941 --> 00:07:54,247
On the first of July, the first bills carry the discount, for about nine in ten eligible households.

65
00:07:56,147 --> 00:08:02,756
In September, the agency's answers come two days late. Billing uses August's, and the next bills catch up.

66
00:08:04,656 --> 00:08:08,026
The log shows one reader of the answers: billing's job.

67
00:08:09,726 --> 00:08:13,208
The head of retail checks the first bills, and closes the ticket.

68
00:08:17,108 --> 00:08:19,535
Here's the solution, on Tomás's map.

69
00:08:20,835 --> 00:08:24,140
Its new parts sit in the application layer, beside billing.

70
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:30,738
Under them, the platform's services, reused, and one new one: sending a file out.

71
00:08:32,638 --> 00:08:36,123
A work package builds the new parts, by the first of July.

72
00:08:37,823 --> 00:08:42,013
And each quality is a requirement, realised by the parts that meet it.

73
00:08:45,913 --> 00:08:53,656
The stations served every traveller. Each lord's journey was his domain's own plan, sent ahead, station by station.

74
00:08:55,356 --> 00:09:03,337
On the data platform, each solution is planned end to end: its context, its qualities, its options, and why, written down.

75
00:09:04,837 --> 00:09:09,243
Most of what it needs is already there. What's new, every team hears ahead.

76
00:09:10,943 --> 00:09:12,827
Next: a road people choose.
